// Branch letterheads for the «گزارش خلاصهٔ پروندهٔ حقوقی» letter type.
//
// The case report is a KIND OF LETTER with its own format (the owner, twice), so
// it uses the letter page and everything on it. What differs is the PAPER: it
// goes out on the BRANCH's letterhead, not the Dubai regional office one that
// `letterhead.ts` carries — a different emblem treatment, and a different box
// number, phone, fax and SWIFT line in the footer. Printing the regional office's
// Dubai address on a branch's legal correspondence is a factual error on a
// document that goes to a court.
//
// WHICH PAPER IS CHOSEN
// ---------------------
// From the ACCOUNT. The customer record carries a branch, so entering the
// account picks the paper — «در صورتی که اکانتی که وارد کردم برای اون شعب بود
// این سربرگ ها ظاهر بشه». With no account, or an account whose branch we have
// no paper for, it falls back to the regional office set, which is what the
// owner asked for: «در حالت عادی اگر چیزی نزده بودم سربرگ تسهیلات باشه».
//
// ADDING THE NEXT BRANCH
// ----------------------
// One entry in `CASE_BRANCHES`, nothing else. Everything downstream — the
// letterhead, the signature line, the dropdown — reads this list, so a branch
// that is added here is added everywhere. («بعدا برای شعب دیگه رو هم اضافه
// میکنم».) Match by `code` (the branch number) and by `aliases` (whatever the
// customer record actually says), because the stored value is free text.
//
// WHERE THE PICTURES COME FROM
// ----------------------------
// Ajman: rendered from the owner's own blank template (`فرمت خلاصه پرونده.pdf`)
// at 288dpi, AS THE PDF PAINTS IT — pulling the raw embedded image streams gives
// the colour channels without their soft masks and prints the marks as dark
// blocks. Murshid Bazar and Al Maktoum: cropped from the scans the owner
// supplied, composited onto white, at their own proportions.
//
// NOTHING HERE IS STRETCHED. The three header boxes render with `object-fit:
// contain` for a case letter, because a letterhead squeezed to fit a box is a
// wrong letterhead — which is exactly what the Ajman emblem was: its artwork is
// 2.55:1 (emblem and branch name SIDE BY SIDE, unlike the two Dubai branches,
// which stack them) and it was being forced into a 1.03:1 box, 40% of its own
// width. That was the «الان اشتباه».

export type CaseBranch = {
  /** the branch number as the bank uses it, e.g. «2898» */
  code: string
  /** what the signature line says, and what the dropdown offers */
  sender: string
  /** Persian/Arabic name, for the UI */
  faName: string
  /** English name as it is printed on the paper itself */
  enName: string
  /** anything a customer record might hold for this branch, lower-cased */
  aliases: string[]
  /** The branch's own paper. ABSENT until the owner supplies that branch's scans
   *  — a branch is listed and signable long before we hold its letterhead, and
   *  printing some other branch's telephone on it would be a factual error. With
   *  no paper the letter keeps the facilities (regional office) set. */
  logo?: string
  name?: string
  footer?: string
  /** Optional header-box override, in MILLIMETRES, when this branch's artwork is
   *  shaped unlike the others. Only the box that actually differs is given; the
   *  rest keep the letter's own layout, which the owner can still drag. */
  logoBox?: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }
}

/** The two standing signatories — neither is a branch, and both print on the
 *  facilities (regional office) paper, which is also what an unknown account
 *  gets: «در حالت عادی اگر چیزی نزده بودم سربرگ تسهیلات باشه». */
export const HOUSE_SENDERS = ['سرپرستی منطقه خلیج فارس', 'دایره تسهیلات اعطایی']

